    "sourceWikitext": "{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Meat recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Bulgaria|Cuisine of Bulgaria ]]\n\n'''Kyufteta''' are Bulgarian roasted meatballs.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]], [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]] (not too fatty)  \n* ¼ lb ground [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:onion|onion]], finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] crumbled bread (preferably at least a day old)\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]  \n* [[Cookbook:pepper|Black pepper]], ground  \n* White pepper, ground\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] dried [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]] (or as much fresh as you like)  \n* 1 tsp grated [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]  \n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Put all the ingredients in a bowl and [[Cookbook:Kneading|knead]] well. \n# Form the mixture into balls approximately 1 [[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] (2.5 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]]) in diameter and flatten them until ½ inch (1.5 cm) thick. \n# Place the balls in a [[Cookbook:Baking Pan|baking pan]] spread with a bit of oil or [[Cookbook:Cooking Spray|cooking spray]] and roast at medium or high heat 15 minutes or until golden brown. \n# Turn the meatballs over and roast another 5 minutes until golden brown on the other side too. \n# When ready immediately remove from pan and place on [[Cookbook:Paper Towel|kitchen paper]] to absorb excess fat. \n# Serve hot with salads, or your favourite sauce. Enjoy!\n\n[[Category:Bulgarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground pork]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground beef]]\n[[Category:Roasted recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cooking spray]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]",
    "isRecipe": true,
